// A DECLARED array length that never folds names the file it was written in
// (DF-232g's residue). The fold half of DF-232g closed Aug 21; this half is the
// diagnostic, and it reported `--> line 9:24` with NO FILE at all — a line
// number and nothing to open.
//
// The rule for a declared length is CODEGEN's, because the length is part of a
// struct's LAYOUT, so the refusal happens with no function or method in scope
// and nothing to read a file off. The expression carries its own source file
// now, stamped by the pass that walks a module's declared types.
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: array length is not a compile-time constant
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: modules/lengthdep/lib.saw:9:
// EXPECT-ERROR-ABSENT: --> line
// COMPILE-FLAGS: --module-path lengthdep={TESTDIR}/modules/lengthdep
import lengthdep.{size}

func main() {
    print(size())
}
